WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.352 --> 00:00:17.145
Anne stayed up all night in her room, thinking about the fact that Gilbert was dying.

2
00:00:18.026 --> 00:00:21.649
The rain beat down and the wind roared terribly outside.

3
00:00:22.430 --> 00:00:29.256
With the possibility of Gilbert gone forever, she knew now that she loved him—she had always loved him!

4
00:00:30.204 --> 00:00:35.246
If she had not been so blind so foolish she could be nursing him now.

5
00:00:37.007 --> 00:00:37.747
Anne sobbed.

6
00:00:38.488 --> 00:00:42.830
Gilbert would never know how she felt; he would die thinking that she did not care.

7
00:00:43.890 --> 00:00:49.453
Anne ached at the thought of life without Gilbert—the black years of emptiness stretching before her!

8
00:00:50.373 --> 00:00:55.755
She cowered down by her window and wished, for the first time in her happy young life, that

9
00:00:55.895 --> 00:00:56.816
she could die too.

10
00:00:58.504 --> 00:01:02.605
Early the next morning, she drove the buggy as fast as she could to the Blythe house.

11
00:01:03.466 --> 00:01:06.046
On the way she met one of the men who worked for Mr.

12
00:01:06.066 --> 00:01:09.447
Blythe. "Do you have any news of Gilbert Blythe?"

13
00:01:09.887 --> 00:01:11.008
she asked breathlessly.

14
00:01:11.028 --> 00:01:13.688
"Yes, I do," the man said.

15
00:01:13.708 --> 00:01:18.490
"He suddenly got much better late last night, and the doctor said he'll recover.

16
00:01:19.210 --> 00:01:20.190
I think he'll be all right."

17
00:01:23.551 --> 00:01:27.232
Anne turned the buggy around and drove slowly back to Green Gables.

18
00:01:28.188 --> 00:01:29.368
She could not think straight.

19
00:01:30.249 --> 00:01:34.210
Her head was buzzing, and she felt more alive than she had in a long time.

20
00:01:35.030 --> 00:01:36.130
This was love!

21
00:01:37.111 --> 00:01:40.732
For Anne it was the most beautiful morning she had ever seen.

22
00:01:41.632 --> 00:01:47.213
The birds were singing, the sun was shining brightly, and best of all, Gilbert was alive.

23
00:01:49.134 --> 00:01:52.735
After his recovery Gilbert visited Green Gables quite often.

24
00:01:53.535 --> 00:01:56.116
Anne did not mention her change in feelings to him.

25
00:01:57.040 --> 00:02:00.202
She believed that Gilbert and Christine Stuart were still a couple.

26
00:02:01.083 --> 00:02:03.345
So Anne tried her best to be just friends.

27
00:02:04.305 --> 00:02:09.429
It was difficult, though, because Anne no longer wanted friendship; she wanted Gilbert's love.

28
00:02:10.410 --> 00:02:14.372
Anne was haunted by a miserable fear that her mistake could never be fixed.

29
00:02:16.374 --> 00:02:20.397
When Gilbert came to Green Gables one afternoon, Anne was waiting for him.

30
00:02:21.477 --> 00:02:25.000
They walked to the graveyard together to put flowers on Matthew's grave.

31
00:02:26.044 --> 00:02:31.628
It was spring again, and the graveyard was particularly beautiful with all the plum trees in bloom.

32
00:02:32.989 --> 00:02:37.832
Anne gently put the flowers on Matthew's grave, and then sat under a tree with Gilbert.

33
00:02:38.633 --> 00:02:41.855
"This place is so beautiful," said Anne softly.

34
00:02:41.875 --> 00:02:43.876
"It's like a dream."

35
00:02:43.896 --> 00:02:46.578
"Do you have any dreams, Anne?"

36
00:02:46.938 --> 00:02:47.659
asked Gilbert.

37
00:02:48.499 --> 00:02:53.683
The tone of his voice sounded different, the way it had sounded that miserable evening in the orchard

38
00:02:53.743 --> 00:02:55.604
at Patty's Place over a year ago.

39
00:02:56.688 --> 00:02:58.209
Anne's heart beat wildly.

40
00:02:58.950 --> 00:03:01.993
Despite trembling inside she gave a light answer.

41
00:03:02.013 --> 00:03:04.395
"Of course, I have dreams!"

42
00:03:04.895 --> 00:03:05.375
she said.

43
00:03:05.395 --> 00:03:07.057
"Everybody has.

44
00:03:07.837 --> 00:03:11.240
We would be as good as dead if we had nothing left to dream about!"

45
00:03:12.902 --> 00:03:14.483
Gilbert turned to look at Anne.

46
00:03:14.503 --> 00:03:16.785
"I have a dream," he said.

47
00:03:16.805 --> 00:03:22.189
"I persist in dreaming it, although it has often seemed to me that it could never come true.

48
00:03:23.150 --> 00:03:27.797
I dream of a nice home with a fireplace in it, a cat and a dog, a big

49
00:03:27.857 --> 00:03:31.800
garden with fruits and vegetables, good friends coming to visit and you!

50
00:03:32.660 --> 00:03:33.781
You are my dream, Anne.

51
00:03:34.481 --> 00:03:35.382
You always have been."

52
00:03:37.783 --> 00:03:40.624
Anne wanted to speak, but she could find no words.

53
00:03:41.705 --> 00:03:44.126
Happiness was breaking over her like a wave.

54
00:03:45.007 --> 00:03:46.168
It almost frightened her.

55
00:03:46.188 --> 00:03:50.310
"I asked you a question over two years ago, Anne," Gilbert said.

56
00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:53.872
"If I ask it again today, will you give me a different answer?"

57
00:03:54.948 --> 00:04:00.110
Anne still could not speak, but she lifted her head and looked steadily into Gilbert's eyes.

58
00:04:01.631 --> 00:04:03.091
She could look nowhere else.

59
00:04:04.032 --> 00:04:07.953
Her eyes shone with love, and Gilbert needed no other answer.

60
00:04:08.834 --> 00:04:11.995
Gilbert dared to smile, and then Anne smiled too.

61
00:04:13.016 --> 00:04:16.157
She was almost afraid to believe that what was happening was true.

62
00:04:16.177 --> 00:04:19.498
"Surely, this is a dream," she thought.

63
00:04:19.518 --> 00:04:28.379
"Gilbert, my love, my true love, telling me he loves me, on a beautiful afternoon in Avonlea "I

64
00:04:31.701 --> 00:04:37.845
thought you loved Christine Stuart," Anne later told him reproachfully, as if she had never gone out with

65
00:04:37.885 --> 00:04:38.566
Roy Gardner.

66
00:04:39.406 --> 00:04:40.287
Gilbert laughed.

67
00:04:40.307 --> 00:04:43.369
"Christine was engaged to somebody in her hometown.

68
00:04:44.209 --> 00:04:45.891
I knew it, and she knew that I knew it.

69
00:04:46.691 --> 00:04:47.812
I was friends with her brother.

70
00:04:48.512 --> 00:04:52.495
He told me his sister was coming to Halifax, and asked me if I would look after her.

71
00:04:53.296 --> 00:04:53.736
So I did."

72
00:04:55.152 --> 00:04:58.834
Gilbert continued, "Christine is one of the nicest girls I've ever known.

73
00:04:59.674 --> 00:05:02.695
I knew college gossip said we were in love, but I didn't care.

74
00:05:03.556 --> 00:05:07.377
After you told me you could never love me, Anne, nothing mattered much to me for a while.

75
00:05:08.298 --> 00:05:09.178
There was nobody else.

76
00:05:10.038 --> 00:05:12.039
There never could be anybody but you for me.

77
00:05:13.240 --> 00:05:16.661
I've loved you ever since that day you broke your slate over my head in school."

78
00:05:16.681 --> 00:05:22.264
"I don't see how you could keep on loving me when I was such a little fool," said

79
00:05:23.468 --> 00:05:29.330
Anne. "Well, I tried to stop," said Gilbert honestly, "and it wasn't easy being told every week by

80
00:05:29.411 --> 00:05:31.591
some busybody that you were almost engaged!

81
00:05:33.372 --> 00:05:34.833
Things only changed a few weeks ago.

82
00:05:34.853 --> 00:05:40.935
I had been really sick—close to dying, the doctor said— when a letter arrived from Phil Gordon.

83
00:05:41.836 --> 00:05:45.037
She told me that there was nothing between you and Roy, and that I should try again.

84
00:05:45.937 --> 00:05:48.739
Well, the doctor was amazed at my rapid recovery after that."

85
00:05:49.619 --> 00:05:51.520
Gilbert smiled lovingly at Anne.

86
00:05:52.756 --> 00:05:54.477
Anne laughed and then shivered.

87
00:05:54.497 --> 00:05:59.198
"I can never forget the night I thought you were dying, Gilbert.

88
00:06:00.258 --> 00:06:06.800
Oh, I knew I knew then how much I loved you and I feared it was too late."

89
00:06:06.820 --> 00:06:13.142
"But it wasn't, Anne, my love," Gilbert said, and he drew Anne close to him and kissed her.

90
00:06:14.063 --> 00:06:18.484
They walked home together in the dusk, happy and together in love.
